# Code owners for blueberry.
#
# There is deliberately NO catch-all `*` rule. Ordinary gameplay PRs need only
# the automated Claude review, so day-to-day work is not gated on one person.
#
# The paths below are load-bearing: they define the environment, the CI gates,
# and the repo's own protection rules. A PR touching any of them needs Talon's
# personal approval IN ADDITION to the ordinary peer review, even though
# every collaborator otherwise has full write access.

# Master context: the rules every review and the constraints check enforce.
/CLAUDE.md                        @talonbaker

# CI/CD: the six required checks and the preview deployment.
/.github/workflows/               @talonbaker

# Repo protection and settings.
/.github/CODEOWNERS               @talonbaker
/.github/stamp-build.sh           @talonbaker
/scripts/apply-repo-settings.sh   @talonbaker

# Phase 0 bootstrap: the single source of truth for the environment.
/scripts/bootstrap.sh             @talonbaker

# Config the required checks read, and hard constraints nothing else asserts.
#
# These are gated for the same reason the workflows are: they decide what the
# CI gates actually mean, and no job re-checks them independently.
#
# .gdlintrc IS the lint gate. Adding a rule to its `disable:` list makes the
# `lint` check pass on code it should reject — verified, not assumed. Gating
# ci.yml but not this file leaves the same hole open one path over.
#
# project.godot carries three of CLAUDE.md §2's non-negotiable constraints —
# the 720x960 viewport with stretch/aspect="keep", worker_pool/max_threads=0,
# and the gl_compatibility renderer that WebGL 2.0 needs. Unlike
# export_presets.cfg, which web-export cross-checks twice, nothing in CI
# asserts any of these, so a PR could quietly change the frame or re-enable
# threads and every check would still pass.
#
# Neither file is touched by ordinary gameplay work, so this does not put
# Talon back in the path of the PRs he wants other people opening.
/.gdlintrc                        @talonbaker
/project.godot                    @talonbaker

# The deterministic gate itself, and the environment every session starts from.
/scripts/check-constraints.sh     @talonbaker
/.claude/                         @talonbaker
